{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires","id":130111,"title":"Sins of the Solar Empires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-10T13:20:41-07:00","id":130111,"title":"Sins of the Solar Empires","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/129683-the-primordial-war?p=130079#post130079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted didn't just kill the soldiers on the field of battle. They went into the cities and murdered the civilians and children and infants, and smashed the eggs, and hunted down the last survivors who weren't even trying to overthrow the Exalted long after they no longer posed any threat whatsoever. That's what genocide means -- cities running with the blood of millions of infants, unarmed refugees run down and shot in the back as they flee, refugee camps nuked from orbit, surrender and pleas for peace refused.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like an interesting motif to weave into campaign.<br /> Would any evidence of these things survive to the Age of Sorrows? I don't mean in underworld, but in Creation. Like mass graveyards, ruined settlements, or even Solar made monuments to the massacres. All of this seems like it would be &quot;cleaned&quot; either by Solar Deliberative, or Uprising Dragon Bloods.<br /> <br /> Did anyone do something like this (would like to hear about it)?<br /> <br /> P.S. Hylden murals under Avernus Cathedral from LoK spring to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","user":"Runelord","date":". 05-10-2014, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T13:31:23-07:00","id":130117,"title":"","content":"I'd love to cover content like this, ancient battle grounds and ruins. I don't like the idea that the Solar Deliberative having developed all the land in Creation, leaving places where such ruins would totally exist, or remnants of such attacks. They could be the remnants of Primordial Wars, to wars between Solars, to the Usurpation, to the wars in the Shogunate Era, to the Balorian Crusades, and even further just regional wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T16:09:49-07:00","id":130787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires#post130111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this seems like it would be &quot;cleaned&quot; either by Solar Deliberative, or Uprising Dragon Bloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's anything I learned from those few months of archaeology classes I took when I was nine, and recently rediscovered from a book I'm reading, it's that it's basically impossible to clear away all evidence of a habitation, even if it amounts to nothing more than unnatural shapes in the landscape where it was cut by and had to grow around roads and buildings.<br /> <br /> I mean, even as a deliberate attempt to destroy it, assuming you can find it, either for being isolated or overgrown or just plain out of the way while your pop density is too low to expand into there.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'd personally view Wyld-Shaping magics as creating a stronger incentive to create entirely new and fairly useful land rather than expand into and altering currently existing ones (if only to preserve areas that haven't been inhabited in the Time of Tumult).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar made monuments to the massacres</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's just silly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T16:28:49-07:00","id":130949,"title":"","content":"I think they would have made monuments to the massacres, because they wouldn't see them as massacres, they'd see them as humanity finally wiping out its enemies. But because of this, the monuments are unlikely to be obviously about massacres, they'd just be something like a statue of a Solar killing some kind of weird gribbly monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T16:37:34-07:00","id":130954,"title":"","content":"That was what I meant, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T16:38:49-07:00","id":130956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires?p=130787#post130787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that's just silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The world says otherwise.<br /> <br /> On one end, you have pyramids of skulls and the victory monuments various wars. On the other, you have the memorials over the Holocaust and other atrocities (which have a tendency to be very creepy).<br /> <br /> The Old Realm doubtlessly raised both kinds, and all those in between.<br /> <br /> Imagine, for example, a great relief of a weeping dragon, marked with glyphs that extol the virtues of some fallen people and the great tragedy of their rejection of the Realm and subsequent annihilation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 05-10-2014, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T23:32:45-07:00","id":131733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires?p=130956#post130956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world says otherwise.<br /> <br /> On one end, you have pyramids of skulls and the victory monuments various wars. On the other, you have the memorials over the Holocaust and other atrocities (which have a tendency to be very creepy).<br /> <br /> The Old Realm doubtlessly raised both kinds, and all those in between.<br /> <br /> Imagine, for example, a great relief of a weeping dragon, marked with glyphs that extol the virtues of some fallen people and the great tragedy of their rejection of the Realm and subsequent annihilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhy would you put this in a role-playing game book? I mean really, I thought we were trying to move away from clubbing the fanbase over the head with the whole 'All First Age Solars = EVIL!' thing here, not make it a dozen times worse and more gauche. You could just make a statue of a Solar king with an inscription of his wars against the Whoever They Were and let the audience draw their conclusion from the lack of Whoever They Were in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T00:15:06-07:00","id":131756,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the Primordial Era, we have humans, Dragon Kings, Lintha, Jadeborn, those funky bird people with the super-long necks, and the Eyeless Face (which is some kind of weird hive-mind behemoth thing), and the people of Heartwind Isle, who were this weird type of human-bio-alchemist. It wouldn't be a terrible idea or anything to mention that there were a couple of other races or groups running around in the era before the Exalted Host overthrew the Primordials. <br /> <br /> But I don't think it should get anything more than a blurb or two. That time is waaay over, and I don't think the books need to waste too much wordcount describing what Creation was like back then.<br /> <br /> That said, a massive, 40 story tall black jade monolith covered in the intricate Moonsilver and Orichalcum runes of a long-extinct language, erected by the First Age Exalted to mollify the spirits of one of the races they exterminated might be kind of cool, especially if in the Second Age nobody has any clue what this really big, really creepy thing was supposed to mean.<br /> <br /> But there probably shouldn't be a lot of these things scattered all over Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T02:08:00-07:00","id":131938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires#post130111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar made monuments to the massacres.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires?p=130787#post130787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that's just silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Persians did this! I saw it in that documentary with Gerard Butler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T02:19:56-07:00","id":131942,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd expect that the Solars built tons and tons of monuments about the Primordial War. Monuments on great battle sites, monuments to famous heroes of the war, monuments to the races they defeated and perhaps races or groups who worked with the Exalts and were thrown down. Not to mention monuments to the dead Primordials, because by remembering their power you remember what an achievement it was to defeat them.<br /> <br /> And they probably maintained and restored those monuments well until the Usurpation. But, during the Shogunate, I imagine that the Dragonblood would have tried to remove any monument to the Solars that they could, so by the time of the game, there are probably a few, but they're very rare, and probably mysterious. Not to mention that over the last 1500 years, they haven't been maintained most likely, so there are probably plenty of ancient feet of statues, or statues too worn down by age and weather to be able to be understood.<br /> And then there's the fact that a lot of memorials were probably in Meru, which few visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T03:32:26-07:00","id":132002,"title":"","content":"You know how Alexander was a fantastic military commander who allowed cities who capitulated to him to live and in fact often treated his defeated enemies with honour and magnaminity.<br /> <br /> And then how sometimes he tore his way inside a city, killed all the men of military age, then sold the women and children into slavery.<br /> <br /> And he didn't really give a shit who knew about either, because both of these acts were not unsurprising for his time.<br /> <br /> That's what Solars were like, I suspect. Sometimes they were fair and honourable in victory, sometimes they wiped entire peoples from the Earth in a screaming fury, and both of these acts were great in their scope and the majesty of their power. And that fits what the Solar is very well. The Solar is a mighty hero in the classical term, a person with the power to change the world and the will to do it, but without any kind of moral necessity to it.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that the Solars would build monuments to their victories, no matter the form they took. Probably dedicated them to Sol Invictus, as well, who in turn probably felt suitably flattered. I mean the UCS was quite happy for the Dragon Kings to sacrifice all those humans to him, a holy genocide resulting in a massive temple dedicated to his name is probably a-ok in his book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 05-11-2014, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T05:15:37-07:00","id":132059,"title":"","content":"I once played a <a href=\"http://www.wizards.com/default.asp?x=dnd/re/20040202a\" target=\"_blank\">swordwraith</a> in a game of <b>Epic Dungeons &amp; Dragons</b>. One of the legends told about him was that he once connected the two oceans of the world by a road paved with the bones of his enemies.<br /> <br /> In a game of <b>Exalted</b> I once ran, the players found a gigantic amber statue resembling a naked Solar warrior (sporting a huge erection, if I remember correctly) and cut out of a single piece of amber. The way this huge piece of amber had been brought about was that the Solar had drained the tree-sap blood of a Greater Elemental Dragon of Wood into a Water Demesne and left it there for a thousand years so that he could build a statue of himself.<br /> <br /> Both the road and the statue are symbols of the the greatness of their creators, but they also represent the crimes committed to create these symbols.<br /> <br /> For some reason, I just thought of a real-world example: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burma_Railway\" target=\"_blank\">The Burma Railroad</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:04:27-07:00","id":132324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires?p=130956#post130956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine, for example, a great relief of a weeping dragon, marked with glyphs that extol the virtues of some fallen people and the great tragedy of their rejection of the Realm and subsequent annihilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya mean, like, &quot;Oh, these guys were super cool, so it's too bad we had to wipe them out.&quot; ?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can get behind that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T11:53:02-07:00","id":132592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires?p=131733#post131733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhy would you put this in a role-playing game book? I mean really, I thought we were trying to move away from clubbing the fanbase over the head with the whole 'All First Age Solars = EVIL!' thing here, not make it a dozen times worse and more gauche. You could just make a statue of a Solar king with an inscription of his wars against the Whoever They Were and let the audience draw their conclusion from the lack of Whoever They Were in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if I remember rightly, one of the developers mentioned that this time around, they were going to leave details of the first age much more vague and open to interpretation. I have to say, I much prefer this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T12:07:01-07:00","id":132602,"title":"","content":"I always wondered what the Varasi are running from, made solars would made sense (sorry had to make a Sins of a Solar Empire joke).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/694-firemage","name":"Firemage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar694_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T03:37:15-07:00","id":133471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/130111-sins-of-the-solar-empires#post130111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like an interesting motif to weave into campaign.<br /> Would any evidence of these things survive to the Age of Sorrows? I don't mean in underworld, but in Creation. Like mass graveyards, ruined settlements, or even Solar made monuments to the massacres. All of this seems like it would be &quot;cleaned&quot; either by Solar Deliberative, or Uprising Dragon Bloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>If not made Triumphal <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_triumphal_arches\" target=\"_blank\">Arches</a> or <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_triumphal_column\" target=\"_blank\">Columns</a> of, if one does it like a roman.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively - and much more sinisterly, a variant of <a href=\"http://www.bootsnall.com/articles/09-05/bone-churches-europe.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> done as memorials or the temple of war and other brutal deities of the Primordial War period. Possibly a temple-manse with the ghosts/spectres of the defeated as servitor force and a hollowed-out version of Oliphem as Guardian for a bonus.<br /> <br /> Those and much more are possibilities for cruel/creepy reminders that not everything the Exalts did for the sake of Creation was pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"ht